How would you secure a Node.js API in production?



⭐ One-line production answer
    “For a production Node.js API, I would use HTTPS, Helmet/security headers, strict CORS, input validation, parameterized database queries, secure password hashing, protected cookies or tokens, rate limiting, secret management, authorization checks, structured security logging, and dependency/security monitoring.”